-- a motion: the permutation it performs, its rate as a function of the temperature, and whether it is
-- proper. The rate is an order of magnitude in inverse seconds and the temperature is in tens of kelvin.
-- A methyl rotation is proper and fast at every temperature anyone works at. A ring flip is proper and
-- its rate crosses the rate an experiment resolves somewhere, which is what a coalescence temperature
-- measures. The exchange of two groups across a mirror plane is not a motion in time at all -- nothing
-- performs it -- and is recorded as improper at every temperature, which an achiral medium supplies and
-- a chiral one does not.
Motion : Type 0
Motion = (p : Nat → Nat) × ((r : Nat → Nat) × Bool)
